Update ICU data to tz database 2026e and fix metazone round-trip failures.

metaZones.txt changes:
- Remap Hawaii_Aleutian golden zone from America/Adak to Pacific/Honolulu.
  CLDR 46 dropped display names for the legacy "Hawaii" metazone; ICU 78.3
  falls back through the mapZone table and formats Pacific/Honolulu as
  "Hawaii-Aleutian Standard Time". The parser then resolves that name via
  the Hawaii_Aleutian golden zone: America/Adak was UTC-11 in 1970 (Bering
  time, before the Aleutians joined Hawaii in 1983), so the round-trip
  landed an hour late for HST, Pacific/Honolulu, Pacific/Johnston and
  US/Hawaii at any pre-1983 date. Pacific/Honolulu is always UTC-10, so
  using it as the golden zone makes the round-trip exact.
- Remap Pacific:Honolulu metazoneInfo from "Hawaii" to "Hawaii_Aleutian"
  so the format step is explicit rather than a fallback.
- Africa/Ceuta and Africa/Freetown: add Europe_Western entry from
  2026-09-20 (tzdata 2026e, ICU-23249 / ICU-23511).

timezoneTypes.txt changes:
- Move CST6CDT, EST5EDT, MST7MDT, PST8PDT from the deprecated usesMetazone
  block to the canonical tzid block so ICU 78 keeps them as first-class
  zone IDs (maint-78 dropped them from that block; restoring them prevents
  lookup regressions in applications that reference these POSIX-style IDs).

zoneinfo64.txt:
- Full replacement with tz database 2026e data (ICU-23249).

